# "If you control a Jace planeswalker token, you can't choose to create a new one when you empower Jace" (the ruling): the
# first Fatehold Charm makes the token with two loyalty, the second puts two more on the same token, so Bot1 has one Jace
# token with 4 loyalty. Each charm draws a card first.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Fatehold Charm
Fatehold Charm
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fatehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Draw a card)
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fatehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Draw a card)
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Hand = Island; Ornithopter; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Fatehold Charm; Fatehold Charm; Black Lotus
